# Input
```css
/* should generate diagnostics */
$name: base;

@layer base {
	@layer base.#{$name} {
	}
}

@layer #{$name} {
	@layer #{$name} {
	}
}

@layer base {
	.a {
		&:hover {
			@layer base {
				color: red;
			}
		}
	}
}

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.scss:5:9 lint/nursery/noSelfNestedLayer ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! The layer base.#{$name} repeats the name of the enclosing layer base.
  
    4 │ @layer base {
  > 5 │ 	@layer base.#{$name} {
      │ 	       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    6 │ 	}
    7 │ }
  
  i Layer names inside a layer block are relative to it, so this creates the sublayer base.base.#{$name}. A sublayer has its own place in the cascade order.
  
  i Rename the layer so it doesn't repeat base, or remove the nested @layer if you didn't mean to create a sublayer.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

